WEBVTT

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.430
And in those interactions,

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:04.897
he's having a version
of what it seems like we have less of,

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.663
but want more of --

00:01:06.663 --> 00:01:09.363
a constructive conversation.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.463
We have more ways than ever to connect.

00:01:12.497 --> 00:01:15.263
And yet, politically, ideologically,

00:01:15.297 --> 00:01:18.497
it feels like we are further
and further apart.

00:01:18.863 --> 00:01:23.063
We tell pollsters that we want
politicians who are open-minded.

00:01:23.563 --> 00:01:26.063
And yet when they change
their point of view,

00:01:26.063 --> 00:01:28.497
we say that they lacked conviction.

00:01:29.263 --> 00:01:31.597
For us, when we're confronted
with information